# Unity.Mathematics over Mathf

Use `Unity.Mathematics` (`math.*`, `float3`, `float4x4`, `quaternion`) instead of `Mathf`/`Vector3` in computation-heavy code. It is SIMD-friendly, Burst-compatible, and avoids `Mathf`'s double-conversion overhead in several methods.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — Mathf + Vector3 in a simulation loop
Vector3 dir = (target - pos).normalized;
float dist = Vector3.Distance(pos, target);
float t = Mathf.Clamp01(elapsed / duration);
pos = Vector3.Lerp(a, b, t);

// ✅ GOOD — Unity.Mathematics
float3 dir = math.normalize(target - pos);
float dist = math.distance(pos, target);
float t = math.saturate(elapsed / duration);
pos = math.lerp(a, b, t);
```

## Concrete mappings

| Instead of | Use |
|------------|-----|
| `Mathf.Clamp01(x)` | `math.saturate(x)` |
| `Mathf.Clamp / Min / Max / Abs / Sqrt / Sin / Cos` | `math.clamp / min / max / abs / sqrt / sin / cos` |
| `Vector3.Distance(a, b)` | `math.distance(a, b)` |
| `v.magnitude` (comparison only) | `math.lengthsq(v)` vs squared threshold |
| `Vector3.Dot / Cross / Lerp / Normalize` | `math.dot / cross / lerp / normalize` |
| `Quaternion.Slerp` | `math.slerp` |
| `Mathf.PerlinNoise` | `noise.cnoise` / `noise.snoise` |

- **Never compare magnitudes with `magnitude`/`length`** — compare `lengthsq` against a squared threshold to skip the sqrt.
- `float3` ↔ `Vector3` convert implicitly and for free; keep the **math** in `float3` and convert only at the Transform boundary.

## When plain `Vector3`/`Mathf` is acceptable

- Thin glue directly against Unity APIs (`transform.position = ...`, physics queries) with no math chain.
- One-off UI/layout calculations outside hot paths.
- Serialized fields in MonoBehaviours/SOs (Inspector shows `Vector3` natively; `float3` also serializes but tooling is weaker).

Do not mechanically rewrite existing working glue code — apply this to new or edited computation code.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] New simulation/math-heavy code uses `Unity.Mathematics` types and `math.*`
- [ ] Distance comparisons use `lengthsq`/`distancesq`, no sqrt
- [ ] Conversions to `Vector3` only at the Unity API boundary
